# Copy to .env and fill in. .env is gitignored, so a fresh clone does NOT have it.
#
# Optional in practice, but ship it anyway. Verified 2026-08-05: the GISC tiled
# basemaps (GISC_BASEMAP_LIGHTCANVAS, COUNTY_IMAGERY_COOK_2025_Project) DO serve
# tiles anonymously — `node scripts/verify-basemaps.mjs` passes no key at all and
# gets HTTP 200 real tiles from both. So the app runs keyless today.
#
# Two things muddy that, both worth knowing before you "simplify" this away:
#   - The tile services' own metadata reports "access":"SECURE", and comments in
#     src/main.tsx and the committed .env both claim the key is needed for the
#     basemap. That claim does not match observed behaviour as of 2026-08-05, but
#     it may have been true earlier — AGOL sharing can be changed out from under
#     this repo, exactly as it can for the feature service (see docs/DATA.md §2).
#   - Routing genuinely needs it, if a profile ever sets enableWalkTime: true.
#     Both profiles have it false today.
#
# So: keyless dev is fine, but keep the key in production builds as insurance.
# If the basemap ever vanishes, re-run verify-basemaps.mjs before assuming it is
# a code problem.
#
# This is a public client key baked into the bundle at build time, which is fine
# — but referrer-restrict it to the deploy domains in the ArcGIS developer
# dashboard. In CI it comes from the VITE_ARCGIS_API_KEY GitHub secret.
VITE_ARCGIS_API_KEY=your_api_key_here
